# Every class epistemics/class_domain.sqlc claims is occupied or epistemics/classes.sqlc finds a
# row in, with how many rows landed there. One row per class, spelled `relation / class`.
#
# `declared` is the CLAIM OF OCCUPANCY, not membership of the roster
#   The roster names all 32 cells, and three of the standings it gives them are different claims.
#   Only `occupied` says a row lands in the class, so only `occupied` is a declaration this fold
#   can be held to. A cell declared `open` or `outside` claims the opposite, and counting it as
#   declared would make reports/integrity.sqlc report every accounted-for empty class as a
#   contract failure, which is the one reading this whole relation exists to prevent.
#
# The two regions are the two directions the standing can be wrong
#   Declared with no row is a class claimed occupied that nothing lands in: the relation stopped
#   producing it, or the claim was never true. A row with nothing declared is a class that filled
#   while its standing says it should not have, which is an `open` class a new document reached or
#   an `outside` class whose population moved. Both are reported by name, and both are the
#   standing going stale rather than the count being wrong.
#
# ⛔ A class declared open and empty has NO row here, and that is correct
#   It is neither declared nor produced, so the full join gives it nothing. The completeness
#   question it belongs to is a different one: that the roster covers its codomain exactly, once
#   per member, which algebra/class_domain.sqlc holds against `pg_enum`. This fold holds
#   occupancy; that law holds the domain.
#
# No verdict
#   A class is counted, not judged, so `rows` is the only box and folds/contract_subjects.sqlc
#   gives it as `answered` with nothing silent or vacuous, the same shape as
#   folds/absence_subjects.sqlc.
#
# Pooled, because occupancy is not a question about evidence
#   The population is the pooled census. Whether anything in this repository computes a class does
#   not depend on which documents are in view; what a chosen set of documents shows is
#   reports/class_census.sqlc's question and carries no contract.
-- epistemics/class_domain.sqlc's occupancy claims against epistemics/classes.sqlc, one row per class.
SELECT coalesce(d.relation, c.relation) || ' / ' || coalesce(d.class, c.class) AS subject,
       d.class IS NOT NULL                                                    AS declared,
       coalesce(c.balls, 0)                                                   AS rows
FROM      (
    SELECT o.relation, o.class
    FROM ( :compose(epistemics/class_domain.sqlc) ) o
    WHERE o.standing = 'exercised'
) d
FULL JOIN (
    SELECT z.relation, z.class, z.balls
    FROM ( :compose(epistemics/classes.sqlc) ) z
    WHERE z.balls > 0
) c ON c.relation = d.relation AND c.class = d.class
